  "headline": "FDA's records trace our diazepam supply to a plant classified OAI 1365 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E6", "D3"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Diazepam has been on FDA's shortage list since 2022-06-15, a span of 52 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Corvale sites use the same NDC 76420031610 labeled by ASCLEMED USA INC.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label identifies the plant as ASCLEMED USA INC. DBA ENOVACHEM (FEI 3001452204).",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2018-09-27 and classified it OAI, with the classification known on 2018-12-26.",
      "cites": ["E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That OAI classification occurred 1365 days before the shortage was first posted on 2022-06-15.",
      "cites": ["E6", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The plant's most recent inspection was 2025-03-05 and resulted in NAI.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based best option is to transfer 33 tablets of 10 mg from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would give Corvale East 10 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    }
  ]
}
